WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.890
- [Narrator] If you are a
female and have certain problems

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.700
with your reproductive organs,

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.820
your doctor may recommend
a robotic hysterectomy

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.593
to remove your uterus.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.173
Your reproductive organs
include your vagina,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.973
cervix,

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:29.703
uterus,

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.853
fallopian tubes,

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:35.983
and ovaries.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.720
You may need a robotic
hysterectomy if you have

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.240
one of the following
diseases or conditions,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.760
heavy or constant uterine bleeding,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.580
anemia and pelvic pain,

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.353
cancer in your uterus,

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:59.083
cervix, or ovaries,

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.263
noncancerous fibroid
tumors in your uterus,

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.780
or slipping and sagging of your uterus

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.540
into your vagina due to weak
or injured pelvic muscles

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.173
and uterine ligaments.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.060
Before your procedure,
and intravenous line,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.640
or IV, will be started.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.580
You may be given
antibiotics through the IV

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.580
to decrease your chance of infection.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.540
You'll be given general anesthesia.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.430
A breathing tube will be inserted

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.570
through your mouth and down your throat

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.113
to help you breathe during the operation.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.620
Your surgeon will make a small incision

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.730
near your belly button and insert

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:48.700
a plastic tube called a port.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.970
Carbon dioxide gas will be pumped

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:54.130
into your abdomen through this port.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.400
The gas will inflate your abdomen,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.680
giving your surgeon more room to see

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.833
and move the surgical tools.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.910
After your abdomen is inflated,

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:08.653
a high-definition camera will
be inserted into this port.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.680
Your surgeon will make
additional port incisions

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.580
for robotic instruments
as well as instruments

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.033
used by patient side assistance.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.940
An assistant will insert all of the

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.363
robotic tools through these ports.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.900
Unlike standard laparoscopic instruments,

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.200
these tools can rotate 360 degrees

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.093
and have more flexibility
than the human wrist.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.360
Seated at a special console,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.740
your surgeon will operate the robotic arms

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.963
and the camera with joystick-like
controls and foot pedals.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.630
A computer will translate
the exact movements

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.390
of your surgeon's fingers into

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.193
precise movements of the surgical tools.

00:02:56.168 --> 00:02:58.280
At the same time,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.990
a high-definition vision
system will provide

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.690
a magnified three dimensional

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.633
stereoscopic view of the surgical area.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:09.670
Depending on your condition,

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.150
you may have a partial hysterectomy

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.883
in which your surgeon
will remove your uterus,

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:18.910
but leave your cervix, fallopian tubes,

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.733
and ovaries in place.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.170
If you have a total hysterectomy,
your surgeon will remove

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:29.933
your cervix along with your uterus.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.810
If you have a radical
hysterectomy, your surgeon may also

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.563
remove your fallopian tubes, ovaries,

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.283
the upper part of your vagina,

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:49.053
as well as nearby tissue such
as your pelvic lymph nodes.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.240
At the end of your procedure,

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.550
the tiny incisions will
be closed with stitches,

00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.803
staples, surgical glue,
or closure tape dressings.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:07.130
After your procedure, your
breathing tube will be removed

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:11.310
and you will be taken to the
recovery area for monitoring.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.560
You will be given pain
medication as needed.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.943
You may continue to receive
antibiotics through your IV.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.710
You may be released from
the hospital the same day

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:24.633
or within one day after the procedure.

